From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kaiyin Zhong <kaiyin@zhong.science>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:10:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] d3d12: don't query the memory budget twice for every
 batch

d3d12_process_batch_residency() read the adapter's memory budget at the
start of every batch and again at the top of its loop, before anything had
changed. On WSL each read is two D3DKMT ioctls to the host, which was about
a third of the CPU time of a glFlush in a small benchmark (glClear + glFlush
on an FBO: 165 us -> 110 us per flush) and ~17% of glxgears' main thread.

Keep the last value in the screen (under submit_mutex) and reuse it at the
start of a batch for up to 10 ms. Making resources resident or evicting them
invalidates it, so a cached value is only used while this process's
residency is unchanged; the loop still re-reads after evicting.

Generated-by: LLM
